# [PROJECT_NAME] Tech Stack & Rules

## Core Technologies
- Next.js App Router (React)
- TypeScript (Strict Mode)
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui
- PostgreSQL & Prisma ORM

## Coding Standards
- Write clean, functional React components.
- Use an API-first backend architecture (`app/api/...` route handlers) to ensure compatibility with future native mobile apps.
- Never use inline CSS; always use Tailwind utility classes.
- Ensure all UI components are mobile-first and highly responsive.
- Do not add random `TODO` comments unless explicitly told to.

## Project Context
This is a live digital showroom/vetrina for local shops (fish markets, butchers, etc.). The merchant experience must be ultra-fast, allowing them to snap photos and publish from a smartphone in seconds. The storefront must support both standalone hosted pages and external embeddable widgets via iframe.
